  "source_provision": "### Statutory Summary Matrix: Section 112A & Grandfathering\n\n| Particulars | Statutory Rule & Conditions | Tax Treatment & Rate |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Asset Category** | Listed equity shares, units of equity-oriented fund, or business trust with STT paid at acquisition and transfer. | Long-Term Capital Asset held for more than 12 months. |\n| **Cost of Acquisition u/s 55(2)(ac)** | Higher of (a) Actual cost of acquisition; and (b) Lower of Fair Market Value as on 31st January 2018 and Full Value of Consideration. | Determines the stepped-up base cost for grandfathering. |\n| **Fair Market Value (31.1.2018)** | Listed Shares/Units: Highest trading price on recognized stock exchange on 31.1.2018. Unlisted Units: Net Asset Value as on 31.1.2018. | Benchmark price for the grandfathering formula. |\n| **Exemption & Tax Rate** | Gains up to ₹ 1,25,000 are exempt. Excess gains are chargeable to tax at 12.5% under Section 112A without indexation. | Flat tax rate plus applicable surcharge and health and education cess. |\n\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> Grandfathering Rule u/s 55(2)(ac): For assets acquired before 1st February 2018, the cost of acquisition is protected by comparing the actual cost with the 31st January 2018 Fair Market Value and actual sale price.\n\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> Indexation Benefit: The benefit of indexation under the second proviso to Section 48 is explicitly not available for capital gains computed under Section 112A."
}
